NUM-25: use Eo = 1 for a curb inlet when the spread is within the gutter

Same fix as for 5.3.0 in Inlet.cpp getCurbInletCapture(): getEo(Sr, T-W, W)
returns NaN when the spread T is narrower than the gutter width W, which makes
the inlet capture 100% of the flow. Use Eo = 1 in that case.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-25_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/Inlet.cpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/Inlet.cpp
index 2738ce5..976850e 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydraulics/Inlet.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydraulics/Inlet.cpp
@@ -297,7 +297,8 @@ double getCurbInletCapture(const Geom& g, double Q, double L) {
     // --- for depressed gutter section
     if (g.a > 0.0) {
         const double Sr = g.sw / g.sx;
-        const double Eo = getEo(Sr, g.t - g.w, g.w);
+        // spread within the depressed gutter: all flow is gutter flow
+        const double Eo = (g.t <= g.w) ? 1.0 : getEo(Sr, g.t - g.w, g.w);
         Se = g.sx + (g.a / g.w) * Eo;                      // HEC-22 Eq(4-24)
     }
 
